1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,673
Venice is sinking.

2
00:00:01,723 --> 00:00:07,928
The most beautiful city ever built on water is slowly losing its fight against the

3
00:00:07,978 --> 00:00:08,233
sea.

4
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:11,950
It sits inside a shallow lagoon on Italy's Adriatic coast,

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,642
spread across more than a hundred islands,

6
00:00:14,692 --> 00:00:18,167
with three narrow inlets connecting it to the open sea.

7
00:00:18,217 --> 00:00:19,363
Beneath the stone,

8
00:00:19,413 --> 00:00:24,881
millions of wooden piles were driven down through mud and clay into a firmer layer.

9
00:00:24,931 --> 00:00:27,142
Starved of oxygen under the water,

10
00:00:27,192 --> 00:00:28,737
the timber never rotted.

11
00:00:28,787 --> 00:00:30,067
It hardened instead.

12
00:00:30,117 --> 00:00:32,060
But the sediment keeps compacting.

13
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:36,984
Industrial groundwater pumping accelerated the sinking until the nineteen seventies.

14
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:38,274
In nineteen sixty-six,

15
00:00:38,324 --> 00:00:41,967
a record surge reached one hundred and ninety-four centimetres.

16
00:00:42,017 --> 00:00:43,406
So Italy built MOSE:

17
00:00:43,456 --> 00:00:47,509
seventy-eight hollow steel gates that rest on the seabed,

18
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:51,900
then swing upward on compressed air to lock the Adriatic out.

19
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:53,243
The shield works.

20
00:00:53,293 --> 00:00:55,060
But Venice still sinks,

21
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:56,640
the sea still rises,

22
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:59,800
and this city is only the first of many.

